// ---------- v2.1 the front lines: every land border between two powers at war is a standing front ----------
// A front is the Voronoi edge between two territories (facNearest) that runs over dry land. Near you (FRONT_NEAR) each side holds a
// zig-zag trench 140 m back from the border - really dug into the ground (terrain edits), with a sandbag parapet, barbed wire out in front,
// machine-gun nests, bunkers and shell craters in no-man's land - manned by riflemen and MG teams who never stop shooting at the other side.
// Dug-in tanks sit behind the trenches; from ladder war level 2 both sides' artillery shells the other trench. When a side runs short of
// tanks, a transport plane flies in from behind its lines and drops new ones by parachute (war level 3+; battles get air drops too).
// Further out (to FRONT_FAR) a front is only gun flashes and smoke on the horizon. Nothing here is saved: fronts follow the war map.
//   fronts: key -> {a,b,fa,fb,pts,n,near,built,S,...}; scanFronts() every 8 s; buildTrenches(F) once; manFront(F,dt) keeps it fighting.
//   drops: transports (in `air`, flag .transport) and falling cargo (`cargo`); airDrop(fid,x,z,n,o) sends one.
